WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.387
A formula for

00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:02.201
the LoRA rank

00:00:02.013 --> 00:00:03.180
you actually need

00:00:03.702 --> 00:00:04.822
Engram derived a

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:05.836
theory for computing

00:00:05.648 --> 00:00:06.756
the minimum LoRA

00:00:06.603 --> 00:00:07.393
rank needed to

00:00:07.204 --> 00:00:08.690
fine-tune on any

00:00:08.502 --> 00:00:09.869
supervised dataset

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:11.215
The idea

00:00:11.263 --> 00:00:12.630
adapter size depends

00:00:12.442 --> 00:00:13.184
on how many

00:00:12.996 --> 00:00:13.998
bits the dataset

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:14.906
takes to encode

00:00:14.718 --> 00:00:15.496
under the base

00:00:15.307 --> 00:00:15.920
model

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:16.943
Some data

00:00:17.015 --> 00:00:18.217
like RL data

00:00:18.335 --> 00:00:18.924
fits in a

00:00:18.736 --> 00:00:19.903
rank one adapter

00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:21.487
In practice

00:00:21.594 --> 00:00:22.761
the method predicts

00:00:22.572 --> 00:00:23.492
the needed rank

00:00:23.304 --> 00:00:24.518
across settings with

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.650
error rates below

00:00:25.462 --> 00:00:26.581
5 percent

00:00:27.102 --> 00:00:28.116
Full story on

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:28.823
the dashboard
